> Do you have to drag dead bodies to the altar to sacrifice?

Some cooperative monsters will do that for you.  Works better if you
are not invisible.  With slow monsters you can't just run and have
them chase so those take a little dancing.  Especially dragons and
giants have to get their themselves because few can pick up their
corpses.  One good thing about instant corpse on altar - It is
always fresh when you get to the altar.

> Is 'sacrificing' a unicorn
> the only way to convert an altar to your god?

Actually it's almost the worst way.  There are 3 colors of unicorn
and offering one of them is a disaster.  Heck, even killing the
wrong color unicorn trashes your luck.

Any other fresh corpse is a better idea than a unicorn.

Then again, once you've learned the table of which unicorn does
what, all you need is careful adherence to that table.

